w the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8309dc45ac43c6642010e744de5a062d6575d48ba85bd642df39dd261f47422.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2b-2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+2b=-2a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cdd0854-261d-5ed4-92ef-477febc75b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234639} {:answer/id #uuid "3eab765d-2302-5205-b5fd-0ada1e027409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234642} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5da092-7603-5a36-a455-4137459af1b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234713} {:answer/id #uuid "dde73660-f588-5765-aec3-a2559c655608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234894} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2c8c3-d49b-55df-8a1c-5ef41ca2446f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234905} :answer-field/id #uuid "959370f5-d157-5592-9470-19e5d767b960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235154}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :quest